  "title": "Erdős Problem #562",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $R_r(n)$ denote the $r$-uniform hypergraph Ramsey number: the minimal $m$ such that if we $2$-colour all edges of the complete $r$-uniform hypergraph on $m$ vertices then there must be some monochromatic copy of the complete $r$-uniform hypergraph on $n$ vertices.\nProve that, for $r\\geq 3$, $ \\log_{r-1} R_r(n) \\asymp_r n, $ where $\\log_{r-1}$ denotes the $(r-1)$-fold iterated logarithm. That is, does $R_r(n)$ grow like $ 2^{2^{\\cdots n}} $ where the tower of exponentials has height $r-1$?",
    "sha256": "fbe18eef2f39ec9bdfcc7b52dcf1ec20df54d51aae185219e2b8207a6105e991",
